  ; ⚠️ The remaining five corners of the SIMD logical group. Opcode 3 of
  ; A64_SIMD_3SAME is eight instructions, not one: `u` picks the half and
  ; `size` -- which is opcode bits here rather than an arrangement -- picks
  ; within it. AND, ORR and BSL were described and the other five were not,
  ; so the group read as a handful of scattered instructions rather than the
  ; square it is:
  ;
  ;        size=0   size=1   size=2   size=3
  ;   u=0  AND      BIC      ORR      ORN
  ;   u=1  EOR      BSL      BIT      BIF
  ;
