  ; ⚠️ PAIRWISE, which is the cross-lane machinery on a real instruction. Each
  ; output lane reads an ADJACENT PAIR -- the first half of the result from
  ; `rn`, the second from `rm` -- so the lane a body reads is a function of the
  ; lane it is computing, and that function is known while the vector expands.
  ;
  ; `(% (* lane-index 2) n)` is not a wrap being papered over. For the output
  ; lanes it applies to, 2i mod n IS 2(i - n/2), which is the index into the
  ; second source; an index that genuinely left the vector would be refused.
  ; The pair is `2i` and `2i + 1`, both reduced the same way.

  (definstruction smaxp_v
    (mnemonic SMAXP_V) (isa aarch64_base) (category float) (format A64_SIMD_3SAME)
