  ; Every lane body works at twice the lane width, so a right shift by the
  ; whole element (`n = esize`, which the encoding allows) needs no special
  ; case: the arithmetic shift fills with the sign and the logical one empties
  ; the lane, exactly as the architecture says, and the rounding constant
  ; `1 << (n - 1)` never overflows. The inserting forms take from `rd` the
  ; bits the shift did not produce, and a shift by the whole element leaves
  ; `rd` untouched.

  (definstruction sshr_v
    (mnemonic SSHR_V) (isa aarch64_base) (category float)
    (format A64_SIMD_SHIFT_IMM)
