  ; ⚠️ The LOWER-HALF (Q = 0) forms of every widening and narrowing `2` form,
  ; derived from it rather than restated. A widening source reads the lower
  ; half -- `(lane r (/ lane-index 2))` where the `2` form adds half the lane
  ; count -- and a narrowing result goes to the low lanes with the high ones
  ; CLEARED, where the `2` form kept them from `rd`. The same index
  ; arithmetic already names the right wide element for a low lane, so the
  ; narrowing change is which arm of the select gets the value. These are
  ; the forms a compiler emits most: `xtn`, `uxtl` (USHLL by zero), `shrn`.
