  ; ⚠️ The Q = 0 (64-bit) ARRANGEMENTS of the same-width instructions, derived
  ; from the Q = 1 forms. The result is the low 64 bits, the upper cleared --
  ; so for an instruction whose low result lanes read only low source lanes,
  ; the Q = 0 formula is the Q = 1 one masked. Permutes and pairwise ops read
  ; lanes at positions set by the lane COUNT, which halves: each arm's
  ; count-dependent constants are halved with it (the modulus, ZIP2's offset,
  ; the half-way comparison). Each gains the exclusion of the arrangement
  ; Q = 0 does not have -- `.1d` (size 3, sz 1, immh 1xxx). The integer
  ; reductions and EXT read the register whole and have bodies of their own;
